<title>KAZAKHSTAN: Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 20.04 pct.</title>
<headline>Kazakh 3-mth T-bill av yield falls to 20.04 pct.</headline>
<dateline>ALMATY 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The average yield on an issue of three-month MKM discount Treasury bills fell to 20.04 at an auction on April 29 from 21.72 at the last auction on April 22, the National Bank said. Details of the auction:</p>
<p>					   Apr 29	     Apr 22</p>
<p> Series number		 KZ43K3110978     KZ43K2407973</p>
<p> Issue volume (million tenge)	     600		  500</p>
<p> Bids (nominal, bln tenge)	   1.26		  2.0</p>
<p> Sold (nominal, million tenge)	    600		784.4</p>
<p> Average price (percent)	    95.23		94.85</p>
<p> Average yield (percent)	    20.04		21.72</p>
<p> Tenor				    91 days	    91 days</p>
<p> Maturity			 July 31, 1997    July 24, 1997</p>
<p>--Almaty Newsroom, +7 3272 509410</p>
